USB: serial: cypress_m8: fix memory corruption with small endpoint

jira KERNEL-1784
cve CVE-2026-63956
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.59.1.el9_8
commit-author Johan Hovold <johan@kernel.org>
commit e1a9d791fd66ab2431b9e6f6f835823809869047
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.59.1.el9_8/e1a9d791.failed

Make sure that the interrupt-out endpoint max packet size is at least
eight bytes to avoid user-controlled slab corruption or NULL-pointer
dereference should a malicious device report a smaller size.

Fixes: 3416eaa1f8f8 ("USB: cypress_m8: Packet format is separate from characteristic size")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org	# 2.6.26
	Reviewed-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
	Signed-off-by: Johan Hovold <johan@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit e1a9d791fd66ab2431b9e6f6f835823809869047)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/usb/serial/cypress_m8.c
diff --cc drivers/usb/serial/cypress_m8.c
index ce9134bb30f3,0b8a4e9d7bc5..000000000000
--- a/drivers/usb/serial/cypress_m8.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/serial/cypress_m8.c
@@@ -445,7 -445,15 +445,19 @@@ static int cypress_generic_port_probe(s
  		return -ENODEV;
  	}
  
